WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.628
Photolithography is how patterns are printed onto silicon chips.

2
00:00:04.733 --> 00:00:07.633
We start with a clean silicon wafer.

3
00:00:07.733 --> 00:00:10.753
A thin layer of oxide is grown on top.

4
00:00:10.866 --> 00:00:15.950
Then a light sensitive coating, called photoresist, is spun on.

5
00:00:16.066 --> 00:00:19.566
A mask with the pattern is lined up above the wafer.

6
00:00:19.666 --> 00:00:22.598
Ultraviolet light shines through the gap,

7
00:00:22.698 --> 00:00:25.038
exposing only part of the resist.

8
00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:29.554
The developer washes away the exposed resist.

9
00:00:29.666 --> 00:00:33.430
Etching removes the oxide that is no longer protected.

10
00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:36.508
Finally, the leftover resist is stripped,

11
00:00:36.608 --> 00:00:38.833
and the pattern is transferred.
